-- record square: One grid square.
--   x: The square's x.
--   y: The square's y.
--   z: The square's floor level.
--   solid: Whether the square blocks movement.
--   solidTrans: Whether the square blocks movement but not sight.
--   light: The square's light level.
--   room: The room name, null outside.
--   building: The building id, null outside.
--   door: The square's door, null when none.
--   window: The square's window, null when none.
--   containers: The square's containers.
--   floor: The full types of the items on the floor.
--   blockN: Whether a step from this square to its north neighbour is blocked: a collide flag with no window, a closed or barricaded door, an intact closed or barricaded window, or a stair top (isBlockedTo).
--   blockW: Whether a step from this square to its west neighbour is blocked: a collide flag with no window, a closed or barricaded door, an intact closed or barricaded window, or a stair top (isBlockedTo).
--   edgeN: Whether a wall, door or window stands on the north edge, open or closed (isSomethingTo).
--   edgeW: Whether a wall, door or window stands on the west edge, open or closed (isSomethingTo).
--   hopN: Whether the square's own north edge is hoppable, has(IsoFlagType.HoppableN) (PZA/1.4, P24-C): a low fence the path follower climbs at a walk though isBlockedTo reads the edge blocked; false beside a solid wall on the same edge.
--   hopW: Whether the square's own west edge is hoppable, has(IsoFlagType.HoppableW) (PZA/1.4, P24-C): a low fence the path follower climbs at a walk though isBlockedTo reads the edge blocked; false beside a solid wall on the same edge.
--   water: The square's water source, null when none (PZA/1.5, P24-G): its first object whose hasWater() holds (a sink, a toilet, a bath, a well, a rain collector, a river, a puddle).
local function enc_square(t)
    if t == nil then return "null" end
    return "[" .. v(t.x) .. "," .. v(t.y) .. "," .. v(t.z) .. "," .. v(t.solid) .. "," .. v(t.solidTrans) .. "," .. v(t.light) .. "," .. v(t.room) .. "," .. v(t.building) .. "," .. enc_portal(t.door) .. "," .. enc_portal(t.window) .. "," .. list(t.containers, enc_container) .. "," .. list(t.floor, v) .. "," .. v(t.blockN) .. "," .. v(t.blockW) .. "," .. v(t.edgeN) .. "," .. v(t.edgeW) .. "," .. v(t.hopN) .. "," .. v(t.hopW) .. "," .. enc_water(t.water) .. "]"
end
PZA.enc.square = enc_square

-- group me: The player's position and gait.
--   x: The world x in tiles.
--   y: The world y in tiles.
--   z: The floor level.
--   dir: The facing direction name.
--   pace: The measured pace in tiles a second.
--   moving: Whether the player is moving.
--   running: Whether the running flag is set.
--   sprinting: Whether the sprinting flag is set.
--   forceRun: The force-run flag read after the frame.
--   forceSprint: The force-sprint flag read after the frame.
--   autoWalk: Whether auto-walk is on.
--   zombiesSeen: The cell's zombie list size, the frame's one walk.
--   zombiesListed: The zombies the frame lists, those alive within the sense radius.
--   hour: The game's hour of day, 0 to 24, as a number.
--   attackers: The zombies attacking the player as the drag-down counts them (PZA/1.4, P24-C): getSurroundingAttackingZombies(), the standing zombies on the player's square and its eight neighbours that target the player within 0.9 tiles in an attack or lunge state; the drag-down kills at three (two at sandbox Strength 1).
--   hitReaction: The player's hit reaction, getHitReaction(), '' when none (PZA/1.4, P24-C): set by every zombie attack that reaches the damage roll, a defended one included; no swing starts while it is set.
--   dragDown: Whether the drag-down death is marked on the player, isDeathDragDown() (PZA/1.4, P24-C).
--   aiming: Whether the player is aiming, isAiming() (PZA/1.5, P24-G): the combat stance an aim holds, or a swing's own while its animation plays; a hit reaction clears it for the reaction's length, a run or a sprint for good.
--   forceAim: The force-aim flag read after the frame, isForceAim() (PZA/1.5.4, P24-T): re-asserted every frame while the stance is held (the game clears it every frame while its toggle-to-aim option is off), so true when the flag survived the frame (not cleared by a run key or a release), while aiming shows whether the update used it; null in logs written before PZA/1.5.4.
--   worn: PZA/1.6 (Plan 24 Task 9 fix 9, review-t18 ruling 5): the body locations the worn clothing covers, each with the bite and scratch defence of the Clothing items worn there summed (getWornItems(), a bag left out), in the order the game lists them; null on every frame whose list equals the last one carried, so a reader keeps the last list it saw (the first frame carries it, [] when nothing is worn), and in logs written before PZA/1.6. Read after an item or damage event, on the frame after the hit reaction rises, changes or ends or the attackers count rises from 0 (a zombie attack turned by the clothing makes a hole and no damage event, PZA/1.6.1), and every tenth frame otherwise. A zombie's scratch rolls under the scratch defence summed over the worn items covering the hit part, a bite under the bite defence (capped at 100): compare a garment's item record with the entry at its loc, an entry with holes above 0 counted as less than its bite and scratch.
--   loadedWidth: PZA/1.7 (Plan 24 Task 9 fix 11): the side in tiles of the square grid of chunks the client holds loaded around the player, getCell():getChunkMap(0):getWidthInTiles() (jar-reads-2 section 13): 104 at a 1280 x 720 window, 152 at 1920 x 1080. A square farther than half of it from the player's chunk on an axis may answer null to getGridSquare, so a walk to it fails no square before any path is asked; a leg of 8 x floor(loadedWidth / 16) - 8 tiles keeps the target inside with a chunk to spare. Carried on the first frame and on a frame where it changed, null otherwise (a reader keeps the last value it saw, as for worn), and in logs written before PZA/1.7.
local function enc_me(t)
    if t == nil then return "null" end
    return "[" .. v(t.x) .. "," .. v(t.y) .. "," .. v(t.z) .. "," .. v(t.dir) .. "," .. v(t.pace) .. "," .. v(t.moving) .. "," .. v(t.running) .. "," .. v(t.sprinting) .. "," .. v(t.forceRun) .. "," .. v(t.forceSprint) .. "," .. v(t.autoWalk) .. "," .. v(t.zombiesSeen) .. "," .. v(t.zombiesListed) .. "," .. v(t.hour) .. "," .. v(t.attackers) .. "," .. v(t.hitReaction) .. "," .. v(t.dragDown) .. "," .. v(t.aiming) .. "," .. v(t.forceAim) .. "," .. list(t.worn, enc_wornLoc) .. "," .. v(t.loadedWidth) .. "]"
end
PZA.enc.me = enc_me

